{"name":"Aquifer","hex":"#e2eced","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aquifer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An underground layer of water-bearing porous stone, earth, or gravel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aquifer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aquifer","blocks":[{"text":"An aquifer is an underground layer of water-bearing material consisting of permeable or fractured rock, or of unconsolidated materials. Aquifers vary greatly in their characteristics. The study of water flow in aquifers and the characterization of aquifers is called hydrogeology. Related concepts include aquitard, a bed of low permeability along an aquifer, and aquiclude, a solid and impermeable region underlying or overlying an aquifer, the pressure of which could lead to the formation of a confined aquifer. Aquifers can be classified as saturated versus unsaturated, aquifers versus aquitards, confined versus unconfined, isotropic versus anisotropic, and porous, karst, fractured, or transboundary."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Groundwater_flow.svg/330px-Groundwater_flow.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aquifer"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Water_seep_from_sandstone_in_Hanging_Garden_SE_Utah.jpg/500px-Water_seep_from_sandstone_in_Hanging_Garden_SE_Utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Water_seep_from_sandstone_in_Hanging_Garden_SE_Utah.jpg/500px-Water_seep_from_sandstone_in_Hanging_Garden_SE_Utah.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water in porous aquifers slowly seeps through pore spaces between sand grains","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWater_seep_from_sandstone_in_Hanging_Garden_SE_Utah.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/MammothCaveNPS.jpg/500px-MammothCaveNPS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/MammothCaveNPS.jpg/500px-MammothCaveNPS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Water in karst aquifers can form subterranean rivers.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMammothCaveNPS.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Major_US_Aquifers_by_Rock_Type.jpg/500px-Major_US_Aquifers_by_Rock_Type.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Major_US_Aquifers_by_Rock_Type.jpg/500px-Major_US_Aquifers_by_Rock_Type.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Map of major US aquifers by rock type","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMajor_US_Aquifers_by_Rock_Type.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Texas_blind_salamander.jpg/330px-Texas_blind_salamander.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Texas_blind_salamander.jpg/330px-Texas_blind_salamander.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Texas blind salamander found in Edwards Aquifer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATexas_blind_salamander.jpg"}],"sounds":{"aquifer":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aquifer.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/2f/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aquifer.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Wodencafe-aquifer.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"ht